--TEST--
a tainted argument at a path parameter does not compile, and the help names `Core\IO::within`, the launderer for a path — `rule:security/launderers-are-sink-named`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:types/qualifiers-tainted-and-secret
// A file name from outside the program is `tainted`.
tainted string $name = "note.txt";

// `Core\IO::read` takes a path, so this line does not compile.
// The error tells you to check the path with `Core\IO::within`.
string $content = Core\IO::read($name);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:8:33
%A
  = help: a file path cannot be `tainted`. Check it with `Core\IO::within($base, $path)`, which returns the path inside `$base` and throws an error for a path that leaves it
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
